<title>SOUTH KOREA: Housing and Commercial Bank '96 net up.</title>
<headline>Housing and Commercial Bank '96 net up.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 1996</p>
<p>		 (In billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)			    2,069	vs   3,863</p>
<p>    Net				    92.24	vs   86.53</p>
<p>    Dividend (par 5,000 won, in cash)</p>
<p>						600	 vs   250</p>
<p>    Operating Revenue		 2,769.68    vs 2,356.26</p>
<p>    Div Register		     Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>    Div Pay			    From Feb 14 to March 14</p>
<p>NOTE - The Housing and Commercial Bank, a state-backed housing loan provider, was publicly listed in March 1996. The government still holds a 47 percent stake.</p>
<p>After the initial public offering, the bank's share capital increased to 47 million at the end of 1996 from 24 million at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>Bank officials said revenues increased due to a greater diversification of loans and more retail business.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
